      "hints": [
        "Use $\\cos\\alpha = \\frac{8}{17}$ and Pythagoras to find $\\sin\\alpha = \\sqrt{1 - \\left(\\frac{8}{17}\\right)^2} = \\frac{15}{17}$.",
        "Calculate $\\tan\\alpha = \\frac{\\sin\\alpha}{\\cos\\alpha} = \\frac{15}{8}$.",
        "Evaluate the sum of reciprocals $\\frac{1}{\\sin\\alpha} + \\frac{1}{\\tan\\alpha} = \\frac{17}{15} + \\frac{8}{15}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Determine the exact value of $\\sin\\alpha$ using the fundamental trigonometric identity with $\\cos\\alpha = \\frac{8}{17}$:\n$$\\sin\\alpha = \\sqrt{1 - \\cos^2\\alpha} = \\sqrt{1 - \\left(\\frac{8}{17}\\right)^2} = \\sqrt{\\frac{289 - 64}{289}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{225}{289}} = \\frac{15}{17}$$",
        "Calculate the exact value of $\\tan\\alpha$:\n$$\\tan\\alpha = \\frac{\\sin\\alpha}{\\cos\\alpha} = \\frac{\\frac{15}{17}}{\\frac{8}{17}} = \\frac{15}{8}$$",
        "Substitute the exact values into the reciprocal expression:\n$$\\frac{1}{\\sin\\alpha} + \\frac{1}{\\tan\\alpha} = \\frac{1}{\\frac{15}{17}} + \\frac{1}{\\frac{15}{8}} = \\frac{17}{15} + \\frac{8}{15}$$",
        "Add the fractions with common denominator:\n$$= \\frac{17 + 8}{15} = \\frac{25}{15} = \\frac{5}{3}$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "ai_rubric": {
